including the pages this video skipped.

171
00:14:54,025 --> 00:14:58,544
You submit the assignment and the lab report on the platform,

172
00:14:58,564 --> 00:15:00,925
and get marks and comments back.

173
00:15:01,325 --> 00:15:07,845
Questions go to the discussion forum, and the grades page shows every mark.

174
00:15:09,365 --> 00:15:17,213
The assignment has three questions. One: a factory has 300 lockstitch machines,

175
00:15:17,233 --> 00:15:20,301
each running 3000 hours a year;

176
00:15:20,321 --> 00:15:25,580
clutch motors average 0.45 kilowatts and servos 0.25,

177
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:32,652
power costs 0.7 yuan a kilowatt-hour, and each retrofit costs 500 yuan.

178
00:15:32,672 --> 00:15:37,831
Find the annual energy and cost saving, the payback,

179
00:15:37,851 --> 00:15:44,305
and the annual CO2 reduction at 0.57 kilograms per kilowatt-hour.

180
00:15:44,705 --> 00:15:44,997
Two:

181
00:15:45,017 --> 00:15:51,464
a fabric weighs 200 grams per square metre with a bending length of 25 millimetres.

182
00:15:51,484 --> 00:15:53,490
Find its bending rigidity.

183
00:15:53,510 --> 00:15:59,101
A strip 5 centimetres long and 20 wide is clamped at one end and pushed,

184
00:15:59,121 --> 00:16:04,088
its other end free to move sideways: at what force does it arch?

185
00:16:04,108 --> 00:16:06,347
Compare that with its weight,

186
00:16:06,367 --> 00:16:12,737
and say how the critical force changes if the clamp is moved to half the distance.

187
00:16:13,137 --> 00:16:18,837
Three: a vendor proposes 8-step robot loading at 98 percent per step,

188
00:16:18,857 --> 00:16:23,893
everything else as in this lecture. Find the unattended rate,

189
00:16:23,913 --> 00:16:26,794
interventions per hour and payback,

190
00:16:26,814 --> 00:16:31,354
and the per-step rate needed for 95 percent unattended.

191
00:16:31,374 --> 00:16:35,498
Then list the data you'd still ask the vendor for,

192
00:16:35,518 --> 00:16:38,317
and recommend whether to pilot it.

193
00:16:38,717 --> 00:16:43,817
Submit the assignment and the lab report on the WenQuest platform.

194
00:16:45,337 --> 00:16:49,146
There's also a ten-question quiz. For example:

195
00:16:49,166 --> 00:16:52,808
two fabrics weigh the same per square metre,

196
00:16:52,828 --> 00:16:58,218
and A's bending length is twice B's. How many times stiffer is A?

197
00:16:58,618 --> 00:17:01,517
Or true or false: for the same fabric,

198
00:17:01,537 --> 00:17:07,201
doubling only the weight while keeping the bending length leaves the droop

199
00:17:07,221 --> 00:17:11,349
and chord angle at a 10-centimetre overhang unchanged.

200
00:17:11,749 --> 00:17:17,329
You get three attempts, and the explanations appear as soon as you submit.

201
00:17:18,849 --> 00:17:20,189
Three things to remember.

202
00:17:20,589 --> 00:17:25,286
One: servo direct drive is the most mature trend;

203
00:17:25,306 --> 00:17:32,312
annual saving is machines times running hours times the power difference,

204
00:17:32,332 --> 00:17:35,489
so the more idle time the better.

205
00:17:35,889 --> 00:17:39,272
Two: cloth has almost no bending rigidity;

206
00:17:39,292 --> 00:17:45,511
it stands only about two bending lengths and buckles before you can push with

207
00:17:45,531 --> 00:17:47,537
a fraction of its weight,

208
00:17:47,557 --> 00:17:50,697
so machines drag fabric with feed dogs,

209
00:17:50,717 --> 00:17:54,829
and workable automation keeps it flat on the table.

210
00:17:55,229 --> 00:18:01,028
Three: a multi-step process runs unattended with probability p to the n,

211
00:18:01,048 --> 00:18:06,605
so each step must beat 99 percent before the robot can be left alone;

212
00:18:06,625 --> 00:18:10,969
and check the numbers in any report on new technology.

213
00:18:11,369 --> 00:18:13,933
The slides, the virtual lab,

214
00:18:13,953 --> 00:18:20,394
the assignment and the quiz are all on the WenQuest learning platform,

215
00:18:20,414 --> 00:18:26,578
at learn.wenquestrobotics.com. Sign up for free and start learning.

